<onlyinclude>The '''ideosphere''' is a metaphor for the environment in which ideas circulate, interact, change and compete for attention. It is sometimes discussed in connection with memetics and cultural evolution. It is not an independently established physical layer of reality.

== Explanation ==
An idea may spread through conversations, texts or media and be changed by each person who uses it. Some ideas are reinforced by institutions, while others disappear from public discussion. The analogy to biological evolution can suggest questions about transmission but does not make ideas equivalent to genes or organisms.

